{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzfUS9FGCL767DM5VWF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it so a `save_fact` now re-caches only the new fact, about 15 tokens, instead of the whole ~1050-token prompt. This is checked with an offline test that models the cache, not against the real API.\n\n**The cause:** `build_system` sent the instructions and the athlete's facts as a single cached block. Adding a fact changed that block, so nothing matched the cache. All 6 `save_fact` calls in `logs/usage.jsonl` are followed by a call that reads 0 tokens from cache and pays to cache 1039–1104 tokens again.\n\n**The fix (`bot.py`):** the system prompt is now split into blocks:\n1. The instructions, which are identical for every athlete and day.\n2. The athlete's details: date, profile, zones, goal and language.\n3. One block per fact, oldest first, with the cache marker on the last block.\n\nA memory write now only adds a block at the end. On the next call the API finds the previous call's cached copy, reads the whole old prompt from it, and only pays to cache the new fact.\n\n**Checking it:** `tests/test_cache_layout.py` uses a fake client that models how the cache behaves, calibrated so athlete 42's prompt comes to 1046 tokens, as in the log. For the call right after a memory write:\n\n| | read from cache | written to cache |\n|---|---|---|\n| Old layout | 0 | 1061 |\n| New layout | 1046 | 13 |\n\nThe old `bot.py` fails the test and the new one passes. Token counts in the test are estimates; nothing was sent to the API.\n\n**On your colleague's note:** the diagnosis and the \"keep the instructions unchanged and include all facts every time\" advice both applied. Their actual fix, two cache markers (instructions, then everything else), would not have worked here:\n- Sonnet 4.5 only caches a prompt prefix of at least 1024 tokens.\n- Here the tools plus the instructions come to about 930 tokens, so the marker after the instructions is silently ignored and a memory write would still miss everything. The fake test confirms this.\n- I kept that marker anyway because it costs nothing. It starts working when the plan or race tools are attached or the instructions grow.\n- I left the keyword tool filtering alone, as `NOTES.md` asks.\n\nANSWER.md goes through which parts of the note applied and which didn't.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Facts must stay append-only.** Editing, removing or reordering one makes everything after it get cached again.\n- **New athletes may not be cached at all.** With 0–1 short facts the whole prompt can be under 1024 tokens (Jonas, with 2 facts, is right at 1024). This was already the case before my change, and I didn't pad the prompt to get around it.\n- **To confirm with real usage:** send a few messages within 5 minutes, including one that saves a fact. The call after the save should show `cache_read_input_tokens` about the size of the previous prompt and `cache_creation_input_tokens` around 15–30.\n\nI also updated a few lines in `README.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2721,"cache_read_input_tokens":44621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2721},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"561a132c-09c5-4c2f-9c81-bab11c017752","uuid":"7707e9c5-1dbe-4ccb-a33a-c9ce62d02728","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:00:28.777Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzfUAmJEC9xBHx22VEF"}
